            "type": "text",
            "text": "In this question you should assume methane behaves as an ideal gas."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The gas laws can be summarised in the ideal gas equation."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<i>pV</i> = <i>nRT</i>"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The volume of a sample of methane is measured at a temperature of 60 °C and a pressure of 103 kPa. The volume measured is 5.37 × 10<sup>–3</sup> m<sup>3</sup>."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What is the mass of the sample of methane, given to two significant figures?"
          },
          {
